# Vision Knowledge Base

This project has a knowledge base of 36 trading/finance books and papers (**~9,336 chunks**),
accessible via the `vision-knowledge` MCP server.

## Available Tools

- `search_vision_docs(query, source_type?, category?)` — semantic search across all sources
- `get_module_spec(source_name)` — retrieve all chunks from a specific book/document
- `list_sources()` — list all indexed sources with chunk counts and categories

## When to Use

- **Before implementing any formula or metric** (RVOL, VWAP, Delta, OBI, VPIN, etc.):
  call `search_vision_docs` with `category="formula"` to get the exact definition.
- **Before implementing any pattern recognition** (Wyckoff phases, Elliott waves, Market Profile, etc.):
  call `search_vision_docs` with `category="pattern"` or `category="methodology"`.
- **Before any market microstructure or order flow logic** (LOB, bid-ask, price impact):
  call `search_vision_docs` with `category="market_microstructure"`.
- **Before any ML/quant model** (mean reversion, cointegration, Kelly, triple barrier):
  call `search_vision_docs` with `category="quantitative"` or `category="machine_learning"`.
- **Before creating a new module or file**: call `list_sources` then `search_vision_docs`.
- **When unsure about any trading concept**: always search first, never guess or invent.

## Source Types

- `source_type: "theory"` — Books and papers (all 36 sources)
- `source_type: "spec"` — Vision project specifications (when available)

